. do ../../sa_first_birth_value_2023.do 

. * 1968-2023 copy of sa_first_birth_value_v1.do (Oct 20 2026). Only changes: i
> nputs are the 1968-2023 files from
. * build_psid_a2h_inputs_2023.do (same items and SHELF definitions, 2021/2023 
> added), output paths, and
. * why-moved codes 10-12 (COVID, evicted, foreclosed; new in 2021) counted as 
> non-space, non-neighbourhood reasons.
. * First-birth house value, mortgage and interstate-move event study, v1 (Oct 
> 18, 2026).
. * Question: do families get space at first birth by moving to cheaper places,
. * so that house value and mortgage barely rise?
. * Design copied from the A2h arm of sa_rooms_first_birth_v2.do (rooms target)
> :
. *   all current adults 18+, PSID longitudinal weight IW, first biological bir
> th,
. *   confirmed-childless never-parents as the control cohort, first birth no e
> arlier
. *   than first adult observation, treated adults reference person or spouse i
> n the
. *   -3/-2 baseline window; Sun-Abraham IW estimator (eventstudyinteract), per
> son
. *   and year fixed effects, age and education indicators, two-year windows,
. *   reference window -3/-2, SE clustered by person.
. * Sample preparation copied from prepare_first_birth_outcomes_v3.do (official
. * year-specific rooms and tenure items merged to the interview year).
. * The A2h filter is evaluated on the rooms sample, as in the rooms target; ea
> ch
. * outcome then keeps its own non-missing rows. Arm own_rep re-runs the v3 A2h
> _own
. * arm with the original logic (filter on the outcome sample) as a replication
>  check.
. * Shelf HOMEVALUER and HOMEMORTOTR are real 2022 USD at the interview year
. * (HOMEVALUER verified equal to official A20 times a year constant, 1999 and 
> 2001).
. * HOMEMORTOTR exists only in 1984, 1989, 1994 and 1999-2019.
